verses.display_text:
And one cried to another, saying:
Holy, holy, holy is the Lord Sabaoth;
all the earth is full of His glory.

And He said, Go, and say to this people:
Hearing, you will hear and certainly not understand;
and seeing, you will see and certainly not perceive.

Curds and honey he will eat;
before he knows or chooses evil,
he will choose the good.

You people who walk in darkness, behold a great light;
you who dwell in a land and shadow of death,
a light will shine upon you.

For the yoke laid upon them has been taken away,
and the rod upon their neck;
for the Lord has shattered the rod of their oppressors,
as in the day against Midian.

For every robe gathered by deceit,
and every garment, they will repay with restitution;
and they will wish that they had been burned with fire.

The spirit of the fear of God will fill him.
He will not judge according to appearance,
nor reprove according to report;

And the ox and the bear will feed together,
and their young will be together;
and the lion and the ox will eat straw together.

And they will certainly do no harm,
nor will they be able at all to destroy anyone upon My holy mountain;
for the whole earth has been filled with the knowledge of the Lord,
as abundant water covers the seas.

You priests, speak to the heart of Jerusalem; comfort her.
For her humiliation is fulfilled, her sin is loosed;
for from the hand of the Lord she has received double for her sins.

A voice of one crying in the wilderness:
Prepare the way of the Lord;
make straight the paths of our God.

And the glory of the Lord will be seen,
and all flesh will see the salvation of God;
for the Lord has spoken.

Like a shepherd, He will shepherd His flock;
and with His arm He will gather lambs,
and comfort those that are with young.

We all, like sheep, have gone astray;
each person has strayed in his own way.
And the Lord delivered him over to our sins.

And I will give the wicked in exchange for his burial,
and the rich in exchange for his death;
for he committed no iniquity,
nor was deceit found in his mouth.

from the toil of his soul,
to show him light and fashion him with understanding,
to justify the righteous one who serves many well;
and he will bear their sins.

Therefore he will inherit many,
and will divide the spoils of the mighty;
for his soul was delivered to death,
and he was numbered among the lawless.
And he bore the sins of many,
and for their sins he was delivered up.

You who thirst, go to the water;
and you who have no silver, go and buy wine and rich food,
and drink without silver or price.

let the ungodly forsake his ways,
and the lawless man his counsels;
and let him return to the Lord, and he will receive mercy;
for He will abundantly forgive your sins.

so it will be with My word, whatever goes out from My mouth:
it will certainly not return until all that I have willed is accomplished;
and I will prosper your ways and My commandments.

For you will go out in gladness, and in joy you will be taught;
for the mountains and the hills will leap, welcoming you with joy,
and all the trees of the field will clap their branches.
